WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.602
Mandy looked closer at Leo’s writing.

2
00:00:05.603 --> 00:00:09.472
"Can you read this, Vinnie?" she said.

3
00:00:09.473 --> 00:00:12.811
But Vinnie was looking at the photo.

4
00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.312
It was glowing blue.

5
00:00:15.313 --> 00:00:19.380
They were standing where the old man had stood!

6
00:00:19.381 --> 00:00:23.743
A well-dressed woman suddenly walked past the children.

7
00:00:23.744 --> 00:00:26.517
She seemed to be in a rush.

8
00:00:26.518 --> 00:00:32.058
As she hurried toward the cathedral door, something fell from her neck.

9
00:00:32.059 --> 00:00:36.659
It landed softly on the open page of Leo’s notebook.

10
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.482
It was a mirror locket.

11
00:00:39.483 --> 00:00:43.352
Mandy noticed the small mirror on the notebook.

12
00:00:43.353 --> 00:00:47.957
"Vinnie, look!" she whispered excitedly.

13
00:00:47.958 --> 00:00:52.497
She picked up the book and held the mirror to the page.

14
00:00:52.498 --> 00:00:55.922
Now Mandy could read the writing!

15
00:00:55.923 --> 00:01:02.536
"The thoughts and ideas of Leonardo di ser Piero da Vinci!" she read.

16
00:01:02.537 --> 00:01:07.587
"Leonardo da Vinci!" the children shouted.

17
00:01:07.588 --> 00:01:13.912
The photo glowed red as they fell down the dark tunnel.

18
00:01:13.913 --> 00:01:17.411
They landed with a thump in the attic.

19
00:01:17.412 --> 00:01:21.992
"Wow, the greatest artist of all time!

20
00:01:21.993 --> 00:01:27.497
It’s too bad we didn’t get to talk to him more!" cried Mandy.

21
00:01:27.498 --> 00:01:31.319
"I could tell he was special," said Vinnie.

22
00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.484
Mandy rolled her eyes.

23
00:01:34.485 --> 00:01:39.940
"Vinnie! Mandy! Come downstairs!" shouted Mom.

24
00:01:39.941 --> 00:01:44.878
The children ran down to their parents, who were still in the kitchen.

25
00:01:44.879 --> 00:01:48.255
"We need to talk," said Mom.

26
00:01:48.256 --> 00:01:52.023
The children sat quietly and listened.

27
00:01:52.024 --> 00:01:55.586
"We’re moving again," began Dad.

28
00:01:55.587 --> 00:01:58.663
"The company needs me in California."

29
00:01:58.664 --> 00:02:03.375
"California!" the children shouted together.

30
00:02:03.376 --> 00:02:07.754
"We just moved here!" said Vinnie.

31
00:02:07.755 --> 00:02:13.312
"I know," said Dad. "But this can’t be helped."

32
00:02:13.313 --> 00:02:18.230
For the next few days, the children were busy packing.

33
00:02:18.231 --> 00:02:21.641
"Kids, would you mind clearing out the attic for

34
00:02:21.642 --> 00:02:24.097
me?" Dad asked one

35
00:02:24.098 --> 00:02:28.916
morning. With heavy hearts Vinnie and Mandy went

36
00:02:28.917 --> 00:02:33.034
upstairs. "I’m sad to leave," cried

37
00:02:33.035 --> 00:02:38.705
Mandy. "Well, at least we got to the end of the album," said

38
00:02:38.706 --> 00:02:41.490
Vinnie. He took the album out

39
00:02:41.491 --> 00:02:45.121
again. Each page had a photo of their

40
00:02:45.122 --> 00:02:51.350
travels. In the pictures the old man was gone, replaced by Vinnie and

41
00:02:51.351 --> 00:02:54.804
Mandy. The objects were not glowing

42
00:02:54.805 --> 00:02:59.174
anymore. "We had some great adventures," said

43
00:02:59.175 --> 00:03:03.543
Vinnie. "And we made many friends," added

44
00:03:03.544 --> 00:03:06.881
Mandy. "What was your favorite

45
00:03:06.882 --> 00:03:09.548
journey?" Vinnie thought for a

46
00:03:09.549 --> 00:03:11.583
moment. "I liked every

47
00:03:11.584 --> 00:03:17.840
one. I learned so much about the world—its different people and their special

48
00:03:17.841 --> 00:03:21.686
cultures." "Me too," agreed

49
00:03:21.687 --> 00:03:24.989
Mandy. "What should we do now?" asked

50
00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:27.717
Vinnie. The children sat and

51
00:03:27.718 --> 00:03:32.113
thought. "Someone else will be living here, right?" said

52
00:03:32.114 --> 00:03:35.128
Mandy. "Maybe they’ll find this

53
00:03:35.129 --> 00:03:39.125
album. Maybe they’ll go on photo travels

54
00:03:39.126 --> 00:03:42.792
too." "Should we leave a note?" asked

55
00:03:42.793 --> 00:03:46.201
Vinnie. "Great idea!" Mandy

56
00:03:46.202 --> 00:03:51.206
said. She grabbed a pen and turned to the first page of the

57
00:03:51.207 --> 00:03:57.640
album. "On our first trip to Egypt, a glowing pyramid called to us . . . ," Mandy

58
00:03:57.641 --> 00:04:02.016
wrote. They finished the note and closed the photo

59
00:04:02.017 --> 00:04:05.919
album. Then they put it in a corner of the

60
00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:10.405
attic. A week later, the family shut the door of their

61
00:04:10.406 --> 00:04:14.368
house. Vinnie and Mandy looked up at the attic

62
00:04:14.369 --> 00:04:19.772
window. Exciting adventures were waiting for whoever would find the album

63
00:04:19.773 --> 00:04:29.508
next. For Vinnie and Mandy, another adventure was about to

64
00:04:29.510 --> 00:05:14.590
begin.

